title: D83 kernel-log change landed after 3 review rounds (first PR through the new review process)
summary: |-
  This is the first PR under T-2026-10-17-003 (fresh-context reviewer plus required Aegis, max 3 rounds, diff-only after round 1, findings verified by the orchestrator). It landed with Aegis APPROVE in round 3. Rounds-to-pass: 3.

  Round 1 found 5+8 Importants, including:
  - a same-boot tamper downgradable to unclean-reboot (no re-stamp on open);
  - the clean-close check reading the file anchor;
  - an unsigned gap row verifying;
  - a clean-close test that could not fail;
  - a p99 that was the max at n=60.

  Round 2 left 2+4 Importants: in-memory-only fault markers, one-directional kernel-key binding, a keyless rotation break, and an interrupted-ack brick. Round 3 closed them. The orchestrator independently re-verified key findings each round and re-ran the suites before commit (gnomon 168, contracts 125).

  Founder decisions along the way: D84 (dev-only no-recovery window) and D85 (file-anchor lag relaxed only across a verified reboot; task created with Aegis's exact rule and 10 fixtures). The process worked: reviewers found real security bugs a single builder pass missed, and the cap held at 3.
symbols_touched:
